This research focuses on the space $\mathcal{C}_\mathrm{NE}$ consisting of all Carathéodory functions from the unit ball $D$ of a Hilbert space $H_1$ to the unit ball $D$ of another Hilbert space $H_2$, that are group-equivariant and non-expansive. It achieves two main goals. Firstly, it provides conditions under which the space of group-equivariant non-expansive operators can be isometrically embedded in a compact space. Secondly, it offers insights into the embedding of $\mathcal{C}_\mathrm{NE}$, and demonstrates that this space is complete and compact if the group is countable, under specific conditions. This study generalizes and unifies previous results in the field, and offers novel findings as well. Furthermore, it contains an appendix that offers further insights into group actions on Hilbert spaces. Lastly, it contains an index that clarifies notations and abbreviations used throughout the paper.  In this paper, the symbol $\ominus$ is employed to denote direct sums of spaces, while $C_\mathrm{p}(D)$ denotes the space of continuous functions, and $T$ denotes the group identity.  Also, the symbol $\sigma$ is employed to denote a group action, while $d_\mathrm{H}}
